## Risk Classification

| Risk class | Present | Evidence | Proof response |
|---|---:|---|---|
| Temporal/state-machine | Yes | `workflow-model.md` scan/get/decode states; parse-before-open and decode-order obligations | TLA+ required for read-only workflow, scan bound, decode order, skip-decode |
| Rust-local invariant | Yes | smart constructors and result contracts in `type-contracts.md` | Verus required for bounded values, typed parse, decode preconditions, read-only capability |
| Bounded state | Yes | scan/preview limits, finite parser classes, bounded record envelope | Kani required where bounded exhaustive state is honest |
| Refinement/type-state | Yes | `HexKey`, `ScanLimit`, `PreviewLimit`, `DecodeMode`, `ReadOnlyStorage` | Flux required where predicates naturally fit refinements |
| Concurrency/interleaving | Limited | read-only/open-existing lock hazard in `hazard-analysis.md` lines 46-51 | Loom required only for read-only open/query handle interleaving; otherwise not applicable |
| Unsafe/UB | Limited | no first-party unsafe in inspected scope, but malformed decode has byte parsing/provenance risk | Miri required for envelope decode malformed inputs only |
| Untrusted input | Yes | argv, hex, numeric limits, malformed envelopes, large values | proptest and cargo-fuzz required for parser/codec/preview hostile surfaces |
| Dependency/supply-chain | Not directly changed by this bead plan | delivery scope identifies source/test additions, not dependency edits | non-behavior waiver candidate for deep supply-chain attestation only |
| Performance/resource | Yes | unbounded scan/preview hazards | bounded-resource obligations via Verus/Kani/proptest/fuzz |
| Release-critical gates | Yes | `moon ci` canonical final gate | included as downstream evidence expectation, not a State 4 proof claim |

## Strategy

1. Use TLA+ for workflows whose correctness depends on temporal ordering: invalid parse must terminate before storage open, scan row count must never exceed limit, read-only operation must not transition to mutation, and envelope decode must validate length/integrity before payload decode.
2. Use Verus as the Rust-core proof spine for pure value-object and type-state contracts: bounded constructors, no unchecked arithmetic/indexing, row-count/preview-length ensures, decode-stage ordering, and capability separation.
3. Use Kani for bounded panic-freedom and finite-state checks over generated/arbitrary inputs. Harnesses must not hardcode a single shape; they must use `kani::Arbitrary` or exhaustive `kani::any()` generators per repository GOD RULES.
4. Use Flux refinements where illegal states are expressible as data predicates: non-empty/even hex bytes, positive capped limits, preview length bounded by cap, and decode stage typestate.
5. Use Loom only for read-only storage/open/query interleavings because other seeds are single-threaded parser/format/decode invariants.
6. Use Miri only for malformed envelope decode byte handling because parser/format/storage capability seeds do not introduce unsafe/FFI/raw pointer behavior.
7. Use proptest and cargo-fuzz for broad CLI/parser/codec/resource surfaces. Behavior assertions remain downstream test states; this plan only names formal/property/fuzz obligations.

